 The fact that platform shooter games like Metroid, Castlevania, Metal Slug and Wario World 4 from over 20 years ago put modern games to shame. You can only shoot horizontally, enemies are linear and you waste your time shooting the same enemies in a conveyor belt fashion. It is excruciatingly painful to play this game when you have to shoot at a mountain of enemies and the damage only targets one at a time. You are constantly on the run trying to open chests and loot and you don't have the time to grab them much less read the descriptions. How is garbage like this even considered positive when it isn't even passable. The music and sounds are loud as hell and generic. The fact that the classes are locked and you have to complete challenges is a scam and solely exists to make you grind just so can't refund this POS game. The fact that almost every modern game is doing this is an absolute joke.", "timestamp_created": 1735740906, "timestamp_updated": 1735740906, "voted_up": false, "votes_up": 2, "votes_funny": 4, "weighted_vote_score": "0.334368616342544556", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1383930480", "reactions": [{"reaction_type": 16, "count": 1}, {"reaction_type": 19, "count": 1}, {"reaction_type": 4, "count": 1}]}]}